# Copy to .env next to compose.yaml on all four boxes, the same file on each. PEERS is required unless MENTAT=1. Unset,
# the other settings take the image's defaults (Dockerfile).

# --- the four boxes -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Their 10G LAN addresses, head first. The head serves the API. With MENTAT=1 (README.md, "Clustering") leave out
# PEERS, IPS and IPS2.
PEERS=192.168.100.10,192.168.100.11,192.168.100.12,192.168.100.13
# Each box's ConnectX address on PCIe root 1 (IPS) and PCIe root 2 (IPS2), in PEERS order.
IPS=10.0.0.1,10.0.0.2,10.0.0.3,10.0.0.4
IPS2=10.0.1.1,10.0.1.2,10.0.1.3,10.0.1.4
# Four boxes cabled in a ring without a switch (gr8/docs/DEPLOY.md): list PEERS in cable order, each box's f0 port
# cabled to the next box's f1 port, and leave out IPS and IPS2.
#SHAPE=ring

# --- the knobs (README.md, "Knobs") ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What to prioritize (README.md, "Pick what to prioritize"). speed: fast mode, faster and not exact (the default).
# context: fast mode, one chat up to 1,048,566 tokens, 16 chats. quality: the exact model, 5 chats.
# EXACT=1, the older name, is now TUNE=quality.
#TUNE=speed
# The longest chat in tokens, prompt and reply together. Every chat slot gets this much KV at boot.
# Unset: 327680 with TUNE=speed, 1048576 with TUNE=context, 262144 with TUNE=quality.
#CAP=327680
# Chats at once. Unset: 32 with TUNE=speed, 16 with TUNE=context, 5 with TUNE=quality. Above 5, the image adds
# GR8_DS_SESS_DRAFTS=1: each chat drafts fewer tokens as more chats write, and none when more than 24 write.
#SESS=32
# 0: the boxes in PEERS. 1: find the other boxes and register the API through the host's mentat daemon, in group GROUP.
#MENTAT=0
#GROUP=gr8-ds41-4x

# --- host directories in place of the named volumes, each owned by uid 1000 ------------------------------------------
#RELEASE_DIR=/srv/ds41/release     # the release, 510.6 GB, on local NVMe
#GR8_HOME_DIR=/srv/ds41/home       # logs, state, Engram's token map and the gen cache (about 80 GB)

# --- faster restarts (README.md, "Switch between this and GLM-5.3 on the same four boxes") ---------------------------
# The loader's gen cache, on: the tensors it computes at load, kept on this box's disk and read back on the next boot of
# the same image. About 80 GB a box in the home volume (79.6 GB), besides the 510.6 GB release. The first boot of an
# image writes it, and so does the first boot after an image change: the loader keeps the two newest images' entries, so
# a box that has run two images holds up to about 160 GB. README.md has the times.
# To turn it off, put a # in front of the EXTRA_ENV line below and run `docker compose up -d` on every box. To free the
# disk, delete the gen-cache directory in the home volume.
EXTRA_ENV=GR8_GEN_CACHE=/var/lib/gr8/home/gen-cache

# --- the image ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A pinned image in place of latest, e.g. ghcr.io/kindlingai/deepseek-v4.1-flash-exlr8-4x-spark:sha-<commit>
#IMAGE=

# --- other -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The release the fetch takes, pinned to a Hugging Face commit (https://huggingface.co/<org>/<repo>@<commit>). The
# image pins the commit measured in README.md.
#RELEASE=https://huggingface.co/kindlingai/deepseek-v4.1-flash-exlr8-native@98076325aaa2c8dfec6095536d69c47bfcfbb3dc
# Files the fetch takes at once
#FETCH_JOBS=8
# Sent only to Hugging Face, for a gated or private repo
#HF_TOKEN=
# Any other gr8 launcher option (gr8/KNOBS.md) works here too, as NAME=VALUE. Engine settings in EXTRA_ENV
# (NAME=value pairs separated by spaces) are added after the recipe's own (Engram, and the TUNE value's settings).
